A: You can use the following code:
if (!$this->hasPermission('edit', $item)) {
    return $this->addError("You don't have permission to edit this item.");
}

This code checks if the current user has the 'edit' permission for the given item. If the user does not have the permission, it adds an error message to the response. If the user has the permission, it does nothing and the item can be edited.
Note that the 'edit' permission is just an example. You should replace it with the actual permission you are checking for.
You can find more information about permissions in the Laravel documentation: https://laravel.com/docs/5.8/permissions

